1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:02,210
Mia spots a tiny hole

2
00:00:02,250 --> 00:00:03,810
in her airplane window.

3
00:00:03,850 --> 00:00:05,330
Her seatmate Otto is sure

4
00:00:05,370 --> 00:00:07,330
it's a manufacturing mistake.

5
00:00:07,370 --> 00:00:08,530
It isn't.

6
00:00:08,630 --> 00:00:09,700
Up at cruising height,

7
00:00:09,740 --> 00:00:12,110
the air outside is too thin to breathe,

8
00:00:12,150 --> 00:00:14,180
so the cabin air is pressurized.

9
00:00:14,220 --> 00:00:15,700
That pressure pushes outward

10
00:00:15,740 --> 00:00:16,930
on every window,

11
00:00:16,970 --> 00:00:18,230
the whole flight.

12
00:00:18,270 --> 00:00:20,040
A window has several panes,

13
00:00:20,080 --> 00:00:21,010
and the hole is drilled

14
00:00:21,050 --> 00:00:22,240
in the middle one.

15
00:00:22,280 --> 00:00:23,280
It lets cabin pressure

16
00:00:23,320 --> 00:00:24,020
into the gap,

17
00:00:24,060 --> 00:00:24,930
so the outer pane

18
00:00:24,970 --> 00:00:26,230
carries the load.

19
00:00:26,270 --> 00:00:27,690
It also lets moisture escape,

20
00:00:27,730 --> 00:00:29,540
so the glass doesn't fog.

21
00:00:29,580 --> 00:00:30,730
Otto leans in,

22
00:00:30,770 --> 00:00:32,830
squints, and goes quiet.

23
00:00:32,870 --> 00:00:33,520
Mia smiles.

24
00:00:33,560 --> 00:00:34,800
Some mistakes are on purpose.

25
00:00:34,840 --> 00:00:36,710
Subscribe so you never miss

26
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:40,140
the next strange fact.
